-- title:
--   Local-cover tables survive writes beyond a common cutoff
-- statement:
--   Let $h\in\mathbb N$, $p=p_h$ be the local prime, $R=p^{2(512h)}$ the candidate count, and $C=p^2$ the number of matrix columns. Suppose memory $\mu$ contains the correct coefficient tables, two histograms, and cover matrix at addresses $a,b_0,b_1,M$. Let $\nu$ agree with $\mu$ at every address below a cutoff $q$. Assume
--
--   $$a+R(1024h)\le q,\qquad b_0+Rp\le q,\qquad b_1+Rp\le q,\qquad M+RC\le q.$$
--
--   Then the same table specification holds in $\nu$:
--
--   $$\operatorname{Data}(\mu,h,a,b_0,b_1,M)\Longrightarrow\operatorname{Data}(\nu,h,a,b_0,b_1,M).$$
--
--   This preservation rule retains all constructed local-cover data across later work above the cutoff.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/c0ldzy17/three-sum-lean/blob/2b639655e07421b9ac743de9090459bab473a7c0/Submission/ThreeSum/LightLocalCoverTables.lean#L62-L84

